Phase-42a router writer family — composition rationale
------------------------------------------------------
Per ADR-004 #9 + the prompt's Locked Decision #2, drive_telemetry
re-uses the snapshotWriter helper's (vehicle_id, ts) per-column
upsert because:

  - drive_telemetry's PK is (vehicle_id, ts) — same shape as the
    *_snapshots family.
  - 10 of 11 routed columns are bindable scalars (float64/bool)
    that bindSnapshotValue accepts directly.
  - The 1 enum-typed column (gear) needs only a thin Stringer
    pre-conversion, not a separate SQL path.
  - drive_id is nullable + never named on insert → backfill
    update path remains independent.

The hybrid wrapper pattern (writer transforms → delegates to
snapshotWriter) is the cleanest expression of "I do exactly one
thing snapshotWriter cannot do: convert a typed proto enum to text".
Mirrors tire_pressure_writer's hybrid pattern minus the duplicated
SQL composition (because string-after-Stringer IS a bindable
scalar).

